Instrumentation-only: compile out every Sauria trace-file writer.

This patch changes no arithmetic, no control flow and no timing. It adds a
`SAURIA_TRACE_FILES` switch, default 0, and puts the two `dump_mac_*` bodies and
their three call sites behind it, and replaces all nine `static std::ofstream`
trace objects with a null-buffer `std::ostream` when the switch is off.

## Why the TPU_V3 adapter cannot compile the source without it

The source writes CSV traces through function-local `static std::ofstream`
objects. Two problems, and they are separate.

**1. The array's writers run unconditionally.** `dump_mac_matrix()` and
`dump_mac_cell()` are reached from the compute process gated only on ordinary
functional conditions (`raw_cswitch_any_a && !raw_cswitch_q_a`,
`local_cswitch_rise`), not on `SAURIA_DEBUG`, which only ever routed `DBG_COUT`.
`dump_mac_cell()` is called from inside the per-processing-element inner loop and
calls `f.flush()` on every invocation: on the 64x64 `int8_64x64` profile that is
up to 4096 flushed writes per column-switch event, into a `trace_sysc/`
directory that may not exist.

**2. A `static` local is shared by every instantiation of the enclosing
template**, so the two matrix engines of a two-core NEO-CORE chip would share one
file handle and one `header_written` flag. CDC-VP's `INTERFACE_CONTRACT.md`
forbids mutable global or static state between instances, in terms that name this
case: "a `static` scratch buffer in a compute kernel is a defect even when tests
pass single-threaded, because SystemC processes interleave at `wait()`
boundaries."

## Why the feeders and the PSM are included, having first been left out

The first version of this patch touched only `sa_array.h`, on the reasoning that
the feeder and PSM writers are each gated at run time on the instance name
containing `NpuTop_std`, and are therefore unreachable from an extracted
composition that never uses that name. The adapter enforces the naming rule, and
the two-instance gate passed.

That reasoning was wrong, and running an actual GEMM is what showed it. The
run-time guard covers the *writes*; it does not cover the **construction**. An
`ofstream` creates its file when it is constructed, and

    static std::ofstream raw_wei_trace("trace_sysc/weight_raw_buf.csv");
    static bool raw_header = false;
    ...
    if (inst_name.find("NpuTop_std") != std::string::npos) { ... }

in `wei_feeder.h` declares the stream *outside* the guard. The first real matrix
job produced `trace_sysc/weight_raw_buf.csv` — an empty file, from a composition
that never uses the reserved name. The two-instance gate had not caught it
because it never ran a job that reached the weight feeder's fetch path.

So the naming rule is now a second line of defence rather than the only one. All
nine writers get the same treatment, in `npu_top.h` too even though `NpuTop` is
excluded, because "no trace file is ever created" is a property that is worth
being able to state without qualification.

The replacement is `std::ostream name(nullptr)`: a stream with no buffer, whose
insertions set `badbit` and write nowhere. It is a one-line substitution per site,
so the surrounding control flow is untouched and the diff is reviewable as a
mechanical transformation rather than as a rewrite.

Offered upstream to the NPU team. Carried downstream meanwhile under the same
policy as the RISC-V VP++ conformance patches: recorded as a file, verified by
content hash, and applied only to a build-tree copy -- never to the source in
place, which other components share.

